        "title": "A Republic Under Pressure",
        "body": "Spain's Second Republic was already strained by land reform, church-state conflict, labor unrest, regional autonomy, and political violence. When the left-wing Popular Front won the 1936 election, conservative officers and right-wing groups accelerated plans for a military uprising.\n\nThe Coup Fails to Finish the Job: The military rebellion began in Spanish Morocco and spread to the mainland in July 1936. It succeeded in some regions but failed in Madrid, Barcelona, and other major cities. Instead of a quick seizure of power, Spain entered a civil war.",
