        "title": "Franco Needs a Bridge",
        "body": "The Nationalists' strongest troops were trapped in Spanish Morocco. With the navy largely loyal to the Republic, Francisco Franco needed aircraft to move the Army of Africa across the Strait of Gibraltar. Germany and Italy supplied planes, pilots, and logistical support.\n\nThe War Internationalizes: The airlift turned a divided coup into a serious Nationalist military campaign. It also revealed the pattern of the war: Spain would become a testing ground for foreign powers, ideologies, aircraft, tanks, and propaganda.",
        "img": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Ju_52_Spanish_Civil_War.jpg/960px-Ju_52_Spanish_Civil_War.jpg",
