        "title": "The Capital Holds",
        "body": "Nationalist forces reached Madrid in November 1936 expecting the capital to fall. Republican militias, regular troops, and newly arrived International Brigades defended the city street by street. Madrid became the symbol of Republican resistance.\n\nA Siege, Not a Capture: Franco's armies failed to take Madrid by direct assault. The front stabilized around the capital, forcing the Nationalists to seek victory elsewhere. Madrid would remain under siege until the final days of the war.",
        "img": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/No_pasaran_madrid_1937.jpg/960px-No_pasaran_madrid_1937.jpg",
