        "body": "Tens of thousands of volunteers from Europe, the Americas, and beyond joined the International Brigades to defend the Republic. Many saw Spain as the frontline of a global struggle against fascism after Hitler and Mussolini backed Franco.\n\nAmericans in the Lincoln Battalion: Around 2,800 volunteers from the United States served, many in the Abraham Lincoln Battalion. They fought despite official US neutrality, making Spain one of the clearest early places where Americans confronted European fascism before World War II.",
