        "body": "Nationalist and Italian-backed forces captured Malaga in February 1937, triggering a mass flight of civilians along the coastal road toward Almeria. The retreat was bombed and shelled, exposing the vulnerability of civilians in modern warfare.\n\nMadrid Still Holds: At Jarama, Nationalists tried to cut the Madrid-Valencia road. At Guadalajara, Italian forces attempted another blow at the capital but were defeated by Republican troops. The battles showed that foreign-backed offensives could still be stopped.",
